\f0  final validation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 That separation will make debugging much easier. In particular, you want to know whether a bad answer came from 
\f1\b retrieval
\f0\b0 , 
\f1\b generation
\f0\b0 , or the 
\f1\b prompt
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Define what the POC must demonstrate\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Before coding, translate the objective into measurable requirements.\
Your POC should demonstrate that a broker can ask questions such as:\
\'93What risks did Apple identify in its latest 10-K?\'94\
\'93Why did NVIDIA's margins change?\'94\
\'93What has been the recent sentiment around Tesla?\'94\
\'93Compare Microsoft's recent stock performance with Amazon.\'94\
\'93What SEC disclosures support the claim that company X faces increasing regulatory risk?\'94\
And receive something resembling:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Answer
\f0\b0 \
NVIDIA reported that gross margin declined primarily because of...\

\f1\b Supporting evidence
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 NVIDIA 10-Q, Item 2 \'97 Management Discussion\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reuters article, August 18, 2026\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 NVIDIA price data, August 1\'9620, 2026\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Confidence / evidence status
\f0\b0 \
Supported by SEC filing and recent market data.\
The critical requirement is that the LLM shouldn't be answering financial questions merely from its pretrained knowledge. The answer should be derived from the retrieved context.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 2. Proposed architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 I would structure the system roughly like this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0              DATA INGESTION\
                   |\
       +-----------+-----------+\
       |           |           |\
     NEWS        PRICES       SEC\
      CSV          CSV        TXT\
       |           |           |\
       +-----------+-----------+\
                   |\
              NORMALIZATION\
                   |\
             LangChain Docs\
                   |\
               CHUNKING\
                   |\
              EMBEDDINGS\
                   |\
                 CHROMA\
                   |\
             VECTOR STORE\
                   |\
                   v\
Broker Question -> Retriever\
                   |\
              Top-K Chunks\
                   |\
                   v\
             RAG Prompt\
                   |\
                   v\
                  LLM\
                   |\
                   v\
       Grounded Financial Answer\
                   |\
                   v\
              DeepEval\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Then place the optimization workflow around that pipeline:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Benchmark Dataset\
       |\
       v\
+------------------+\
| RAG Experiments  |\
+------------------+\
       |\
       +-- chunk_size\
       +-- overlap\
       +-- top_k\
       +-- temperature\
       +-- top_p\
       +-- max_tokens\
       |\
       v\
    DeepEval\
       |\
       v\
Best RAG Configuration\
       |\
       v\
GEPA Prompt Optimization\
       |\
       v\
Optimized Prompt\
       |\
       v\
Final RAG System\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 The important architectural decision here is that 
\f1\b RAG configuration optimization and prompt optimization are distinct experiments
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 3. Phase 1 \'97 Normalize the three datasets\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Don't dump the three raw files directly into Chroma.\
Create a common document representation.\
Something like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Document(\
    page_content="...",\
    metadata=\{\
        "source_type": "news",\
        "ticker": "NVDA",\
        "company": "NVIDIA",\
        "date": "2026-08-15",\
        "source": "Reuters",\
        "url": "...",\
    \}\
)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 For SEC data:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Document(\
    page_content="...",\
    metadata=\{\
        "source_type": "sec",\
        "ticker": "NVDA",\
        "company": "NVIDIA",\
        "filing_type": "10-K",\
        "filing_date": "2026-03-01",\
        "section": "Risk Factors",\
    \}\
)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 And prices:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Document(\
    page_content=(\
        "NVDA trading data for 2026-08-15: "\
        "open 182.10, high 185.40, low 180.25, "\
        "close 184.75, volume 142000000."\
    ),\
    metadata=\{\
        "source_type": "price",\
        "ticker": "NVDA",\
        "date": "2026-08-15",\
    \}\
)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 This metadata will become extremely useful later.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 4. Treat price data differently from text\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is one area where I would deviate from a simplistic RAG implementation.\
News and SEC filings are naturally suited to semantic embeddings.\
Raw OHLCV price records are not.\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 AAPL 204.10 208.33 203.44 207.81 67389231\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 doesn't have much semantic meaning to an embedding model.\
Instead, transform price data into meaningful financial statements or calculate statistics before embedding them.\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Apple (AAPL)\
Period: August 1\'9631, 2026\
\
Starting close: $X\
Ending close: $Y\
Return: +4.7%\
Highest close: $Z\
Lowest close: $W\
Average volume: ...\
Volatility: ...\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Better still, maintain a small 
\f1\b structured analytics layer
\f0\b0  for price questions.\
That gives you a hybrid architecture:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Question\
   |\
   +---------------------+\
   |                     |\
Semantic information   Quantitative information\
   |                     |\
Chroma                 Pandas/Python\
   |                     |\
News + SEC             Price calculations\
   |                     |\
   +----------+----------+\
              |\
              v\
             LLM\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 This will give you substantially better answers to questions such as:\
\'93How has Apple performed compared with Microsoft over the past 30 days?\'94\
Rather than hoping an embedding search happens to retrieve the correct daily price rows.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 5. Phase 2 \'97 Establish a baseline RAG system\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Do 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  start with GEPA.\
First establish a boring, predictable baseline.\
For example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 BASELINE_CONFIG = \{\
    "chunk_size": 1000,\
    "chunk_overlap": 150,\
    "top_k": 5,\
    "temperature": 0.0,\
    "top_p": 1.0,\
    "max_tokens": 800\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 Then implement:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 Question\
   
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f3 \
Embedding\
   
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f3 \
Chroma similarity search\
   
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f3 \
Top 5 chunks\
   
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f3 \
Prompt\
   
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f3 \
LLM\
   
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f3 \
Answer\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 A baseline prompt might conceptually say:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 You are a financial intelligence assistant for brokerage professionals.\
\
Answer the question using only the supplied context.\
\
Requirements:\
- Do not introduce facts unsupported by the context.\
- Clearly distinguish facts from interpretation.\
- Cite the supporting sources.\
- If the context is insufficient, say so.\
- When discussing financial changes, explain the evidence supporting\
  the conclusion.\
- Keep the response concise enough for a broker preparing for a\
  client discussion.\
\
CONTEXT:\
\{context\}\
\
QUESTION:\
\{question\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 That gives you something measurable before optimization begins.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

